{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"dwarf_sled","model_identifier":"dwarf_sled","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"## dwarf_sled\n\nDwarf supply sled (E7).\n\n- Cubes: 58 (9 rotated). Texture 128x256, 1 px per 2 units (half density so it fits 256 px), embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -27.1..27.5, y 0.0..49.1, z -113.0..44.1 (size 54.6 x 49.1 x 157.1 u = 154 x 138 x 442 cm).\nDwarf supply sled: a low, square, heavy sled (55 x 38 x 95 u, about 1.5 x 1.1 x 2.7 m, plus the drawbar) on two iron-shod timber runners with upturned fronts, timber crossbeams, a dressed stone bed, iron corner brackets and timber rails with a team-colour stripe. The load (stone blocks, ore, ingots, crates, a keg) is covered by an oiled brown tarp tied down with three chains hooked to iron rings on the rails. A driver's perch sits at the front against the load; a stout drawbar with an iron ring is dragged by an ox. No wheels (dwarves do not build roads). Faces -Z.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 55 x 38 x 88 u from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = -1 (the drawbar is not solid).\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `sled` (pivot on the ground at the centre) > `runner_r` / `runner_l`, `drawbar` (pivot at the front beam), `tarp` (hinge along the back top edge) > `chain_r_0..2` / `chain_l_0..2` (the hanging side runs of the chains).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the drawbar ring (45 u up, 109 u ahead of the centre), at the ox's harness/collar trace point; `slot_rider` on the perch (hips at 17 u, facing -Z); `slot_crew_1` / `slot_crew_2` = walking escort beside the sled (40 u out, front right and back left); `slot_cargo` on the stone bed (12.5 u up) for D6 loads when the tarp is off.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` (drag, no wheels) designed for 28.4 u/s (0.8 m/s, a loaded ox's pull), 1.2 s per cycle = one ox stride pair: the sled lurches and scrapes forward, pitching slightly, and the chains jangle.\n\n**Key times:** `use` (unload) 2.2 s: the chains are unhooked and swing loose (0-0.4 s), then the tarp is thrown back over the rear (0.45-1.5 s); key 1.5 s (load uncovered, unloading can start). Play reversed to cover up again. `idle` the chains sway gently. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with jangling chains. `destroyed` holds: the right runner snaps off and lies flat, the sled drops onto its broken side, a chain parts, the tarp slides askew and the drawbar drops to the ground.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 3 | loop |\n| `move` | 1.2 | loop |\n| `use` | 2.2 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.8 | hold |\n"},"description":"## dwarf_sled\n\nDwarf supply sled (E7).\n\n- Cubes: 58 (9 rotated). Texture 128x256, 1 px per 2 units (half density so it fits 256 px), embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -27.1..27.5, y 0.0..49.1, z -113.0..44.1 (size 54.6 x 49.1 x 157.1 u = 154 x 138 x 442 cm).\nDwarf supply sled: a low, square, heavy sled (55 x 38 x 95 u, about 1.5 x 1.1 x 2.7 m, plus the drawbar) on two iron-shod timber runners with upturned fronts, timber crossbeams, a dressed stone bed, iron corner brackets and timber rails with a team-colour stripe. The load (stone blocks, ore, ingots, crates, a keg) is covered by an oiled brown tarp tied down with three chains hooked to iron rings on the rails. A driver's perch sits at the front against the load; a stout drawbar with an iron ring is dragged by an ox. No wheels (dwarves do not build roads). Faces -Z.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 55 x 38 x 88 u from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = -1 (the drawbar is not solid).\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `sled` (pivot on the ground at the centre) > `runner_r` / `runner_l`, `drawbar` (pivot at the front beam), `tarp` (hinge along the back top edge) > `chain_r_0..2` / `chain_l_0..2` (the hanging side runs of the chains).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the drawbar ring (45 u up, 109 u ahead of the centre), at the ox's harness/collar trace point; `slot_rider` on the perch (hips at 17 u, facing -Z); `slot_crew_1` / `slot_crew_2` = walking escort beside the sled (40 u out, front right and back left); `slot_cargo` on the stone bed (12.5 u up) for D6 loads when the tarp is off.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` (drag, no wheels) designed for 28.4 u/s (0.8 m/s, a loaded ox's pull), 1.2 s per cycle = one ox stride pair: the sled lurches and scrapes forward, pitching slightly, and the chains jangle.\n\n**Key times:** `use` (unload) 2.2 s: the chains are unhooked and swing loose (0-0.4 s), then the tarp is thrown back over the rear (0.45-1.5 s); key 1.5 s (load uncovered, unloading can start). Play reversed to cover up again. `idle` the chains sway gently. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with jangling chains. `destroyed` holds: the right runner snaps off and lies flat, the sled drops onto its broken side, a chain parts, the tarp slides askew and the drawbar drops to the ground.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 3 | loop |\n| `move` | 1.2 | loop |\n| `use` | 2.2 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.8 | hold |\n","resolution":{"width":128,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"runner_r_shoe","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[20.0,0.0,-40.0],"to":[25.0,1.5,42.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[22.0,0.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[0,174,2.5,174.75],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[2,167,43.0,167.75],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[3,174,5.5,174.75],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[43,167,84.0,167.75],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[54,0,56.5,41.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[57,0,59.5,41.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"8257a77c-a890-5a53-ba6d-e3474138d8a0"},{"name":"runner_r_beam","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[20.25,1.5,-40.0],"to":[24.75,6.5,42.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[22.0,0.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":